# Environment files.
# The scaffold only ships `*.local`, which misses a plain `.env` — the most
# common filename. This repo is PUBLIC (GitHub Pages requires it on the free
# plan), so a committed secret is a published secret. Only .env.example, which
# contains no real values, is tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
